@welcoMattic right, the logout lands on the user's next request, and the risk is the record expiring first. It's kept for `session.gc_maxlifetime` as read by the process handling the provider's POST, and on a lazy firewall nothing builds the session there, so that's the php.ini value (1440s) even when `framework.session.gc_maxlifetime` or the handler's `ttl` says a day. Past that, the user comes back to a working login. I was wrong in my first comment when I said this lifetime is always `session.gc_maxlifetime`.

